WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.328
Prompt your coding

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.307
agent without making

00:00:02.119 --> 00:00:02.885
a sound

00:00:03.414 --> 00:00:04.263
A new Claude

00:00:04.074 --> 00:00:05.241
Code plugin reads

00:00:05.053 --> 00:00:05.819
your lips through

00:00:05.631 --> 00:00:06.491
the webcam

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.526
The lip reading

00:00:07.338 --> 00:00:08.552
model runs locally

00:00:08.364 --> 00:00:09.519
on Apple Silicon

00:00:09.543 --> 00:00:10.522
so no audio

00:00:10.333 --> 00:00:11.406
is recorded and

00:00:11.218 --> 00:00:12.267
no video leaves

00:00:12.079 --> 00:00:12.797
the Mac

00:00:13.318 --> 00:00:14.343
It uses Auto

00:00:14.155 --> 00:00:15.829
AVSR's visual model

00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:16.773
with two hundred

00:00:16.584 --> 00:00:18.141
fifty million parameters

00:00:17.964 --> 00:00:18.978
trained on three

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.122
thousand two hundred

00:00:19.945 --> 00:00:21.018
ninety one hours

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:21.549
of video

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:23.685
Accuracy is modest

00:00:23.591 --> 00:00:24.393
with a twenty

00:00:24.204 --> 00:00:25.277
point three percent

00:00:25.089 --> 00:00:26.020
word error rate

00:00:25.832 --> 00:00:26.869
on its benchmark

00:00:27.058 --> 00:00:27.624
so you can

00:00:27.436 --> 00:00:28.166
train it on

00:00:27.978 --> 00:00:28.803
your own lips

00:00:28.615 --> 00:00:29.487
with about one

00:00:29.299 --> 00:00:30.419
hundred phrases

00:00:30.942 --> 00:00:31.956
Full story on

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:32.663
the dashboard
